  "body": "If we have one pending and one waiting task and abort them both, then the queue gets stuck with one pending task forever and gets blocked\r\n\r\n```js\r\nimport PQueue, {AbortError} from 'p-queue';\r\n\r\nconst queue = new PQueue({concurrency: 1});\r\n\r\nconst controller1 = new AbortController();\r\nconst controller2 = new AbortController();\r\n\r\ntry {\r\n\tconst task1 = queue.add(({signal}) => fetch('https://sindresorhus.com', {signal}), {signal: controller1.signal});\r\n\tconst task2 = queue.add(({signal}) => fetch('https://example.com', {signal}), {signal: controller2.signal});\r\n\r\n\r\n          setTimeout(() => {\r\n                  controller1.abort();\r\n                  controller2.abort();\r\n          \r\n                  queue; // Size: 1  Pending: 1\r\n          }, 0)\r\n\r\n        await task1;\r\n        await task2;\r\n} catch (error) {\r\n\tif (!(error instanceof AbortError)) {\r\n\t\tthrow error;\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```",
